W44-143: W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_AUTO_MIN_DISTANCE bisection
================================================================================

DATE: 2026-05-20
COMMIT: TBD (W44-143 ship commit on origin/main)
BASELINE: 11a00293 (W44-142 SHIPPED, current main)
HOST: lilith (water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM)
WALL: 1340.8 seconds (22.3 minutes, 30 cells × 5 candidates = 150 encodes)

PURPOSE
-------

Test whether widening the W44-135 lower bound on the W44-124
`dct32_keep` auto-discriminator can close the codec_wiki d=1.6/1.8
SSIM2 regression cluster surfaced by W44-141 / attributed by W44-142.

Background:

  - W44-124 (`bc9f71eb`) shipped the auto-discriminator with NO
    distance gate.
  - W44-134 ledger refresh measured collateral SSIM2 regressions at
    codec_wiki d=4/5/6 (-0.64 to -1.43) and d=0.8/1.0 (-0.41 to -0.52)
    under unconditional firing.
  - W44-135 (`2b9c98d0`) narrowed the auto-fire to distance ∈ [2.0, 3.5]
    to close those collateral regressions.
  - W44-141 ledger refresh surfaced a NEW codec_wiki cluster at e8/e9
    d=1.2/1.6/1.8 (SSIM2 -0.62 to -0.72 vs W44-134).
  - W44-142 (`11a00293`) attributed e9 d=1.2 to W44-140 fade-band and
    closed THAT cell, BUT documented that d=1.6/1.8 are NOT W44-140-
    attributable — they regressed because W44-135 SHUT OFF the W44-124
    lift on codec_wiki at d=1.6/1.8 (those distances sit OUTSIDE the
    [2.0, 3.5] band).

W44-143 hypothesis: lowering MIN_DISTANCE from 2.0 to e.g. 1.6 might
re-enable the W44-124 lift on codec_wiki at d=1.6/1.8 (closing those
cluster cells) while preserving:

  - W44-142 fix at d=1.0..1.4 (codec_wiki low-d cells stay byte-identical
    when MIN is set above 1.4)
  - W44-124 wins at d=2.5/3.0 (preserved trivially — bisect MIN values
    are all ≤2.0)
  - W44-135 protection at d=4/5/6 (MAX_DISTANCE stays at 3.5, untouched)
  - W44-140 wins on terminal d=1.0-1.6 (terminal m3=13.85 fails m3 gate
    regardless of MIN_DISTANCE → terminal byte-identical across all
    candidates)
  - Photo byte-identical (photo ed>=0.16 fails ed gate)

VARIANTS TESTED
---------------

Per-cell 5-mode bisect (`JXL_W44_143_MIN_DISTANCE` env-var override
added in `vardct/encoder.rs`):

  min2_0 : MIN=2.0 (current main W44-135 baseline)
  min1_8 : MIN=1.8
  min1_6 : MIN=1.6
  min1_4 : MIN=1.4
  min1_2 : MIN=1.2

All variants share the SAME content discriminator: m3>=60 AND ed<0.05
(W44-124 constants — unchanged) AND `distance <= MAX (= 3.5)` (W44-135
ceiling — unchanged). Only the FLOOR moves.

CELLS (30)
----------

CW_LOWD : codec_wiki × {e8, e9} × {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.6, 1.8, 2.0}   (12)
CW_HIGHD: codec_wiki × e7 × {2.5, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0, 6.0}              ( 5)
TERM    : terminal × {e8, e9} × {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.6, 1.8, 2.0}     (12)
PHOTO   : 1418519 × e7 × 4.0                                       ( 1)

ACCEPTANCE GATES
----------------

G1: codec_wiki d=1.6/1.8 — ≥2 of 4 cells improve by ≥+0.20 SSIM2
G2: codec_wiki d=1.0-1.4 — worst Δssim2 > -0.20 (W44-142 wins preserved)
G3: codec_wiki d=3 e7 — |Δssim2| < 0.05 (W44-124 win preserved)
G4: codec_wiki d=4/5/6 e7 — worst Δssim2 > -0.10 (W44-135 protection)
G5: terminal d=1.0-1.6 e8/e9 — worst Δssim2 > -0.05 (W44-140 protection)
G6: photo — Δbytes == 0 (gate must not fire on CID22 photo)

