PARETO ANALYSIS
---------------

**min1_4 STRICTLY DOMINATES min1_6** at the same gate-pass rate (6/6):
adds 2 wins (e8/e9 d=1.4 +0.31 each) on top of min1_6's 3 wins, with
no additional regressions.

**min1_2 fails G2** — re-introduces the W44-135-protected d=1.2 SSIM2
regression on top of the new wins. Confirms W44-135's original 2.0
floor was correct to protect d=0.8/1.0/1.2 (just too wide — should
have been 1.4).

**min1_8 fails G1** — only closes 1 of 4 target cells.

The single remaining regression (e8 d=1.8 -0.18 SSIM2) is unavoidable
at any floor ≤ 1.8: the e8/e9 split at d=1.8 reflects buttloop iter
asymmetry (e8 has 2 iters, e9 has 4 iters). e9 settles to +0.72 SSIM2
under the lift while e8 starves to -0.18. Same structural pattern as
the W44-140 EPF fade design — pure threshold tightening cannot
resolve it; would require effort-aware sub-gating which is out of
W44-143 scope.

DECISION
--------

**SHIP min1_4** (`W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_AUTO_MIN_DISTANCE: f32 = 1.4`).

Net W44-143 effect vs W44-142 main:
- 5 NEW SSIM2 wins on codec_wiki cells in the d=1.4..1.8 band
  - codec_wiki e8 d=1.4: +0.314 SSIM2  (+2.4% bytes)
  - codec_wiki e9 d=1.4: +0.314 SSIM2  (+2.1% bytes)
  - codec_wiki e8 d=1.6: +0.615 SSIM2  (+4.1% bytes)
  - codec_wiki e9 d=1.6: +0.615 SSIM2  (+3.6% bytes)
  - codec_wiki e9 d=1.8: +0.718 SSIM2  (+2.8% bytes)
- 1 minor SSIM2 regression at e8 d=1.8 (-0.183 SSIM2, +3.0% bytes)
- Preserves W44-142 W44-124 W44-135 W44-140 protections (every other
  cell byte-identical)

