DO NOT
------

- DO NOT lower `W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_AUTO_MIN_DISTANCE` below 1.4 — the
  bisect is conclusive that d=1.2 cells regress SSIM2 -0.27 to -0.43
  under the W44-124 dct32_keep lift. W44-142's EPF seed suppression
  owns d ∈ [1.0, 1.5) on a different code path; the two mechanisms
  must stay isolated.

- DO NOT raise `W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_AUTO_MIN_DISTANCE` above 1.6 — at
  MIN=1.8 only 1 of 4 target cells closes (e9 d=1.8 +0.72). The d=1.4
  and d=1.6 cells (4 wins, +0.31 to +0.62 SSIM2) stay locked out.

- DO NOT widen `W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_AUTO_MAX_DISTANCE` above 3.5 — that
  was W44-135's original protection for the d=4/5/6 -0.64 to -1.43
  SSIM2 cluster. Bisect didn't measure d>3.5 cells under min1_4 (out
  of scope) but the MAX ceiling is independent of MIN floor.

- DO NOT try to close the e8 d=1.8 -0.18 SSIM2 residual via a
  per-effort sub-gate without a paired bisect — the e8/e9 split is
  structural (buttloop iter asymmetry, same pattern as W44-140 fade
  design). Likely requires a separate "use uniform-4 sharpness at e8
  d=1.8" lever or per-iter effort scaling, not a MIN_DISTANCE move.

- DO NOT respawn FMA precision claims (RULED OUT by user 2026-05-19).

